Core's protections below apply as soon as you confirm, and approval for every
command from each pane's next turn. From then until the restart this session
also has: approved and allow-listed commands stay inside this session's sandbox
(commands can write to the current folder, /private/tmp) and network off for
agent commands. The rest of the rows above take effect when you restart Corbanu
Terminal (you can restart right after saving); until then this session keeps its
current sandbox, network, environment, model-key and child-agent settings, apart
from Core's protected-path denials and what is listed as in force, and commands
already running keep the permissions they started with. Your config.toml is
not modified.
